Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: Intel: sof_es8336: restore Infinix amplifier on playback restart

STOP mutes the amplifier without changing the DAPM state. A subsequent
START can therefore leave playback running with the amplifier muted.
Requeue the existing 70 ms GPIO work for playback START, RESUME and
PAUSE_RELEASE while the speaker route is powered. Limit to the tested
board; capture and other boards are unchanged. This ports the previously
hardware-tested local 1.0.1 fix to the pinned upstream source.
Link: https://github.com/thesofproject/linux/issues/5967

Research candidate; not submitted or hardware-qualified as a new release.

---
diff --git a/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_es8336.c b/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_es8336.c
--- a/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_es8336.c
+++ b/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_es8336.c
@@ -137,6 +137,12 @@
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_START:
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_PAUSE_RELEASE:
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_RESUME:
+		/* STOP can mute the amp without cycling DAPM speaker power. */
+		if (priv->headphone_gpio_follows_speaker &&
+		    substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK &&
+		    !priv->speaker_en)
+			queue_delayed_work(system_dfl_wq, &priv->pcm_pop_work,
+					   msecs_to_jiffies(70));
 		break;
 
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_PAUSE_PUSH:
